foundation.question_text:
Calculate the area of this irregular quadrilateral block of land.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,2.25);
\coordinate (C) at (6,2.25);
\coordinate (B) at (2,3.75);
\coordinate (D) at (3.5,0);
\coordinate (E) at (2,2.25);
\coordinate (F) at (3.5,2.25);
\draw[thick] (A) -- (B) -- (C) -- (D) -- cycle;
\draw[thick] (A) -- (C) node[pos=0.8, above] {$16\text{ m}$};
\draw[dashed] (B) -- (E) node[midway, left] {$4\text{ m}$};
\draw[dashed] (D) -- (F) node[midway, right] {$6\text{ m}$};
\draw (E) rectangle ++(0.25,0.25);
\draw (F) rectangle ++(-0.25,-0.25);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Calculate the area of this irregular block of land.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (P) at (0,2.7);
\coordinate (R) at (6.6,2.7);
\coordinate (Q) at (2.5,4.8);
\coordinate (S) at (4,0);
\coordinate (E) at (2.5,2.7);
\coordinate (F) at (4,2.7);
\draw[thick] (P) -- (Q) -- (R) -- (S) -- cycle;
\draw[thick] (P) -- (R) node[pos=0.85, above] {$22\text{ m}$};
\draw[dashed] (Q) -- (E) node[midway, left] {$7\text{ m}$};
\draw[dashed] (S) -- (F) node[midway, right] {$9\text{ m}$};
\draw (E) rectangle ++(0.25,0.25);
\draw (F) rectangle ++(-0.25,-0.25);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A field is surveyed along a baseline $AB$. Perpendicular offsets are measured on one side as shown. Calculate the area of the field.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);
\coordinate (B) at (6,0);
\coordinate (C) at (2.5,0);
\coordinate (P) at (2.5,2);
\draw[thick] (A) -- (P) -- (B) -- cycle;
\draw[dashed] (P) -- (C) node[midway, right] {$8\text{ m}$};
\node[below] at (1.25,0) {$10\text{ m}$};
\node[below] at (4.25,0) {$14\text{ m}$};
\draw (C) rectangle ++(-0.25,0.25);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Calculate the area of the surveyed land parcel shown below.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);
\coordinate (B) at (7.5,0);
\coordinate (X) at (2,0);
\coordinate (Y) at (5,0);
\coordinate (P) at (2,1.5);
\coordinate (Q) at (5,2.5);
\draw[thick] (A) -- (P) -- (Q) -- (B) -- cycle;
\draw[dashed] (P) -- (X) node[midway, left] {$6\text{ m}$};
\draw[dashed] (Q) -- (Y) node[midway, right] {$10\text{ m}$};
\node[below] at (1,0) {$8\text{ m}$};
\node[below] at (3.5,0) {$12\text{ m}$};
\node[below] at (6.25,0) {$10\text{ m}$};
\draw (X) rectangle ++(0.25,0.25);
\draw (Y) rectangle ++(0.25,0.25);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Find the perimeter of this triangular parcel of land, correct to the nearest metre.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);
\coordinate (B) at (6,0);
\coordinate (C) at (2.5,0);
\coordinate (P) at (2.5,3);
\draw[thick] (A) -- (P) -- (B) -- cycle;
\draw[dashed] (P) -- (C) node[midway, right] {$8\text{ m}$};
\node[below] at (1.25,0) {$6\text{ m}$};
\node[below] at (4.25,0) {$8\text{ m}$};
\draw (C) rectangle ++(-0.25,0.25);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

development.question_text:
A field survey was conducted along a baseline $AB = 60\text{ m}$. Offsets to the north boundary are $14\text{ m}$ at $15\text{ m}$ along $AB$ and $18\text{ m}$ at $40\text{ m}$ along $AB$. A single offset to the south boundary is $16\text{ m}$ at $30\text{ m}$ along $AB$. Calculate the total area of the field.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);
\coordinate (B) at (6,0);
\coordinate (X) at (1.5,0);
\coordinate (Y) at (4,0);
\coordinate (Z) at (3,0);
\coordinate (P) at (1.5,1.4);
\coordinate (Q) at (4,1.8);
\coordinate (S) at (3,-1.6);
\draw[thick] (A) -- (P) -- (Q) -- (B) -- (S) -- cycle;
\draw[thick] (A) -- (B);
\draw[dashed] (P) -- (X) node[midway, left] {$14\text{ m}$};
\draw[dashed] (Q) -- (Y) node[midway, right] {$18\text{ m}$};
\draw[dashed] (S) -- (Z) node[midway, right] {$16\text{ m}$};
\node[below] at (0.75,0) {$15\text{ m}$};
\node[below] at (2.75,0) {$25\text{ m}$};
\node[below] at (5,0) {$20\text{ m}$};
\draw (X) rectangle ++(0.2,0.2);
\draw (Y) rectangle ++(0.2,0.2);
\draw (Z) rectangle ++(0.2,-0.2);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Calculate the perimeter of this quadrilateral block of land $PQRS$, correct to the nearest metre.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (P) at (0,0);
\coordinate (R) at (6,0);
\coordinate (Q) at (2.4,2);
\coordinate (S) at (2.4,-2.5);
\coordinate (M) at (2.4,0);
\draw[thick] (P) -- (Q) -- (R) -- (S) -- cycle;
\draw[thick] (P) -- (R);
\draw[dashed] (Q) -- (S);
\node[left] at (P) {$P$};
\node[above] at (Q) {$Q$};
\node[right] at (R) {$R$};
\node[below] at (S) {$S$};
\node[below] at (1.2,0) {$8\text{ m}$};
\node[below] at (4.2,0) {$12\text{ m}$};
\node[left] at (2.4,1) {$6\text{ m}$};
\node[left] at (2.4,-1.25) {$9\text{ m}$};
\draw (M) rectangle ++(0.25,0.25);
\draw (M) rectangle ++(0.25,-0.25);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
